# Cursor Cloud specific instructions

These notes apply only to Cursor Cloud agents. Follow the shared
[agent instructions](../../AGENTS.md) for development state, checks, and process cleanup.

## Toolchain

Use the tool versions pinned in [mise.toml](../../mise.toml) and follow
[First checkout](../../docs/operations/development.md#first-checkout) for setup.
Run commands in a login shell so the provisioned toolchain is on `PATH`, or use
`mise exec --` as the development runbook describes. Before installing dependencies,
check `node --version` and `vp --version` against the pinned tool versions.

## Running the web app

Run `vp run dev --home-dir .supaterm` from the repository root and retain its terminal session. Read the
actual ports and pairing URL from the dev-runner output. Pair the browser with that
URL before testing the UI.

The explicit home isolates a regular clone's state in `.supaterm/userdata`; linked worktrees
already select that directory by default. Never run against `~/.supaterm/userdata`
or set `VITE_HTTP_URL` or `VITE_WS_URL` for browser development; Vite proxies the backend
through the browser's origin. Follow [Test data](../../AGENTS.md#test-data) for fixtures
when working in a linked worktree.

Use the [Replay provider](../../docs/operations/development.md#replay-provider) to test
agent turns without a paid provider account. Pair the browser automation available in
your environment with the startup URL.

## Android native builds

Follow the [mobile development guide](../../apps/mobile/README.md#development). Use
`vp run mobile:install android [device-id]` to install the native client for this
checkout's fingerprint before starting Metro. The helper reuses the local build cache
and builds when needed.

To prepare an Android build without an attached device, run
`vp run mobile:install android --prepare --abi x86_64` (or `--abi arm64-v8a` for an ARM
device). If the VM cannot run an emulator and no device is available, report that
runtime verification could not be completed.
